# Frontend React/TypeScript Applications Rules

## React/TypeScript Standards
- Use TypeScript for all new code
- Prefer functional components with hooks over class components
- Use proper TypeScript types and interfaces
- Avoid `any` type - use proper typing or `unknown`
- Use React.memo() for performance optimization when needed

## Project Structure
- `live-chatter/` - Real-time audio chat application
- `survey-hub/` - Survey management and analytics dashboard
- Each app follows similar structure:
  - `src/components/` - Reusable UI components
  - `src/pages/` - Page-level components
  - `src/hooks/` - Custom React hooks
  - `src/integrations/` - External service integrations
  - `src/lib/` - Utility functions
  - `src/utils/` - Helper functions

## Component Guidelines
- Use shadcn/ui components from `components/ui/`
- Follow atomic design principles
- Keep components focused and single-purpose
- Use proper prop interfaces with TypeScript
- Implement proper error boundaries

## State Management
- Use React hooks (useState, useEffect, useContext) for local state
- Use Supabase client for server state management
- Implement proper loading and error states
- Use React Query or SWR for data fetching when needed

## Styling
- Use Tailwind CSS for styling
- Follow the established design system
- Use CSS modules or styled-components for complex styling
- Maintain responsive design principles

## Performance
- Use React.lazy() for code splitting
- Implement proper memoization with useMemo and useCallback
- Optimize bundle size with tree shaking
- Use proper key props in lists

## Testing
- Write unit tests for components using React Testing Library
- Test user interactions and accessibility
- Mock external dependencies
- Maintain good test coverage

## Accessibility
- Use semantic HTML elements
- Implement proper ARIA attributes
- Ensure keyboard navigation works
- Test with screen readers

## Build and Development
- Use Vite for build tooling
- Follow the established ESLint and Prettier configuration
- Use proper environment variables
- Implement proper error handling and logging
